{% set local_problem %}
<p>Arab's hillside location and abundant tree coverage create a perfect storm for clogged gutters. Oak leaves pile up in fall. Pine needles accumulate year-round. And when gutters clog on sloped terrain, the consequences are worse than on flat land — overflow water gains velocity as it runs downhill toward your foundation.</p>

<p>Many Arab homeowners put off gutter cleaning because it's dangerous, time-consuming, and frankly unpleasant. Climbing ladders on uneven hillside terrain is risky, and reaching all sections of gutters on a multi-level home requires specialized equipment.</p>

<p>The cost of neglecting gutters far exceeds the cost of cleaning them. Foundation repairs in the area average $5,000-15,000. Fascia board replacement runs $1,000-3,000. A couple of professional cleanings per year is a bargain compared to those alternatives.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our gutter cleaning process is thorough and professional:</p>

<p><strong>1. Debris Removal:</strong> We remove all leaves, pine needles, twigs, and sediment from your gutters by hand, ensuring nothing gets pushed into downspouts.</p>

<p><strong>2. Downspout Flushing:</strong> We flush each downspout with water to ensure it's completely clear and flowing properly. Clogged downspouts are a common cause of gutter overflow that many DIY cleaners miss.</p>

<p><strong>3. Exterior Cleaning:</strong> We wipe down the outside of visible gutters, removing dirt, mildew, and staining so your home looks its best.</p>

<p><strong>4. Inspection:</strong> We check for loose hangers, damaged sections, separating seams, and signs of fascia rot. If we find issues, we'll let you know and provide repair options.</p>

<p><strong>5. Cleanup:</strong> We bag all debris and leave your property cleaner than we found it. You won't find piles of leaves on your lawn.</p>
{% endset %}

